---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Origin: check who made an image, and whether AI was involved"
  description="Reads the Content Credentials attached to a photo and shows who signed it, what they claim, and what changed since. Runs in your browser. Nothing is uploaded."
  path="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="private-badge">Runs in your browser, nothing is uploaded</p>
      <h1>Who actually made this image?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Cameras from Leica and Sony, and tools from Adobe and OpenAI, now attach a signed record to
        the files they produce. Drop an image here and Origin reads that record: who signed it, what
        they say it is, and whether it has been changed since.
      </p>

      <div class="drop" id="drop" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Choose an image to check">
        <input type="file" id="file" accept="image/*" hidden />
        <div class="drop-inner">
          <span class="drop-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="drop-title">Drop an image, or click to choose one</p>
          <p class="drop-note">JPEG, PNG, WEBP, AVIF and TIFF. Large files are fine, they are read locally.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="try">
        No signed image to hand?
        <button type="button" id="try-sample">Try a signed example</button>
        <span class="try-note">A test file from the C2PA project.</span>
      </p>

      {/* Stated before any result appears, not after. A tool that reads as an
          AI detector will be believed as one, so the limit comes first. */}
      <div class="honesty">
        <h2>What this can and cannot tell you</h2>
        <div class="honesty-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>It can prove</h3>
            <p>
              That a named signer attached specific claims to this exact file, and whether a single
              byte has changed since. That part is cryptography, not opinion.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>It cannot prove</h3>
            <p>
              That the claims are true. A credential says what its signer says. It is only worth as
              much as your trust in whoever signed it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>It is not an AI detector</h3>
            <p>
              Nothing here guesses. If a file has no credentials, the honest answer is that we know
              nothing about it, and that is what you will be told.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" id="result" hidden aria-live="polite"></section>

  <section class="wrap article">
    <h2>What are Content Credentials?</h2>
    <p>
      They are a tamper evident record attached to a file, built on an open standard called C2PA. The
      record lists what the file is, what was done to it, and which software or device was involved.
      The whole thing is signed, so any later change to the pixels breaks the signature and can be
      detected.
    </p>
    <p>
      The point is not to catch fakes. It is to let honest files carry their own history, so a photo
      from a news agency can show where it came from rather than asking you to take it on faith.
    </p>

    <h2>Who adds them</h2>
    <ul class="who">
      <li><strong>Cameras</strong> Leica M11-P and SL3-S, Sony Alpha bodies with the firmware enabled, some Nikon models.</li>
      <li><strong>Editing tools</strong> Adobe Photoshop and Lightroom, when Content Credentials are switched on.</li>
      <li><strong>AI generators</strong> OpenAI image output, Adobe Firefly, Microsoft Designer, Google tools using SynthID alongside C2PA.</li>
      <li><strong>Platforms</strong> LinkedIn displays them, and others are adding support.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why most images have nothing</h2>
    <p>
      Adoption is early. Most phone cameras do not sign, most apps strip metadata when saving, and
      every social platform that re-encodes an upload destroys the credential unless it deliberately
      preserves it. A missing credential is the normal case, not a red flag.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is the part other tools get wrong. An image with no credentials is not suspicious. It is
      just an ordinary file, and no tool, including this one, can tell you how it was made.
    </p>

    <h2>What a broken signature means</h2>
    <p>
      If a file carries credentials but the check fails, something changed after signing. Often that
      is innocent, such as a resize or a re-save by software that did not understand the credential.
      It does mean the claims can no longer be trusted for that file, because they describe a
      version of it that no longer exists.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 52px 0 8px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 18px 0 16px;
    max-width: 16ch;
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .drop {
    margin-top: 30px;
    border: 2px dashed var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--panel);
    padding: 44px 24px;
    text-align: center;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      border-color 0.15s ease,
      background 0.15s ease;
  }

  .drop:hover,
  .drop.is-over {
    border-color: var(--seal);
    background: var(--seal-soft);
  }

  .drop-mark {
    display: block;
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    margin: 0 auto 14px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--seal);
    position: relative;
  }

  .drop-mark::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 9px 9px auto auto;
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--panel);
  }

  .drop-title {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .drop-note {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .try {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .try button {
    margin-left: 6px;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--seal);
    color: var(--seal);
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 0 0 1px;
  }

  .try-note {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    margin-left: 6px;
  }

  .honesty {
    margin-top: 40px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 26px;
  }

  .honesty h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .honesty-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
    gap: 22px;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .honesty h3 {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .honesty p {
    margin-top: 7px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .article {
    padding-top: 60px;
  }

  .article h2 {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    margin-top: 36px;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .article h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .article p {
    margin-top: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .who {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .who li {
    background: var(--panel);
    padding: 13px 17px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .who strong {
    display: block;
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  /* The result is built at runtime, so these cannot be scoped. */
  .result-head {
    display: flex;
    gap: 22px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding-top: 48px;
  }

  .thumb {
    width: 128px;
    height: 128px;
    flex: none;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--sunk) repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, #f0efe9, #f0efe9 6px, #e8e6dd 6px, #e8e6dd 12px);
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .verdict {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .verdict-tag {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border-radius: 100px;
  }

  .v-none .verdict-tag {
    background: var(--neutral-soft);
    color: var(--neutral);
  }
  .v-tampered .verdict-tag {
    background: var(--danger-soft);
    color: var(--danger);
  }
  .v-ai-generated .verdict-tag,
  .v-ai-assisted .verdict-tag {
    background: var(--ai-soft);
    color: var(--ai);
  }
  .v-camera .verdict-tag {
    background: var(--ok-soft);
    color: var(--ok);
  }
  .v-edited .verdict-tag,
  .v-signed .verdict-tag {
    background: var(--seal-soft);
    color: var(--seal);
  }

  .verdict h2 {
    font-size: 1.625rem;
    margin: 12px 0 10px;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .verdict-why {
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  /* The confidence line is never optional. It is the honest caveat, so it sits
     with the verdict rather than somewhere further down the page. */
  .confidence {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--sunk);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(190px, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-top: 26px;
  }

  .fact {
    background: var(--panel);
    padding: 14px 16px 16px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .fact-label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faint);
  }

  .fact-value {
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  /* The chain of custody, which is the thing worth looking at. */
  .chain {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 26px 0 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 22px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .chain::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 5px;
    top: 8px;
    bottom: 8px;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--line);
  }

  .chain li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 9px 0;
  }

  .chain li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -22px;
    top: 16px;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 2px solid var(--seal);
  }

  .chain-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .chain-soft {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  .section-title {
    margin-top: 32px;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .warn-soft {
    background: var(--seal-soft) !important;
    color: var(--seal) !important;
  }

  .warn-list {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--danger-soft);
    color: var(--danger);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .raw {
    margin-top: 26px;
  }

  .raw summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .raw pre {
    margin-top: 12px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #d9d6c9;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 14px 16px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-height: 420px;
  }

  .loading,
  .failure {
    margin-top: 48px;
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 22px 24px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .spinner {
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    border: 2px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-top-color: var(--seal);
    border-radius: 50%;
    animation: spin 0.7s linear infinite;
    flex: none;
  }

  @keyframes spin {
    to {
      transform: rotate(360deg);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .result-head {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .thumb {
      width: 100%;
      height: 180px;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { interpret, type Reading } from '../lib/provenance';

  const drop = document.getElementById('drop')!;
  const input = document.getElementById('file') as HTMLInputElement;
  const result = document.getElementById('result')!;

  const TAGS: Record<Reading['verdict'], string> = {
    none: 'nothing found',
    tampered: 'signature failed',
    'ai-generated': 'ai generated',
    'ai-assisted': 'partly ai',
    camera: 'captured',
    edited: 'edited',
    signed: 'signed',
  };

  const CONFIDENCE: Record<Reading['confidence'], string> = {
    proven:
      'This one is mathematical. The signature covers the exact bytes of the file, and they no longer match.',
    claimed:
      'This is what the signer states, not something we checked independently. It is only as trustworthy as the signer.',
    unknown: 'No credentials means no information. Treat this as neither evidence for nor against anything.',
  };

  function esc(value: string): string {
    return value
      .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
      .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
      .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
      .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
      .replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
  }

  function show(html: string): void {
    result.hidden = false;
    result.innerHTML = html;
  }

  function fact(label: string, value: string | null): string {
    if (!value) return '';
    return `<div class="fact"><div class="fact-label">${label}</div><div class="fact-value">${esc(value)}</div></div>`;
  }

  function render(reading: Reading, thumbUrl: string, fileName: string, raw: unknown): string {
    const chain = reading.steps.length
      ? `<h3 class="section-title">What was done to it</h3>
         <ol class="chain">${reading.steps
           .map(
             (s) => `<li><div class="chain-label">${esc(s.label)}</div>${
               s.software ? `<div class="chain-soft">${esc(s.software)}</div>` : ''
             }</li>`,
           )
           .join('')}</ol>`
      : '';

    const ingredients = reading.ingredients.length
      ? `<h3 class="section-title">Built from</h3><ol class="chain">${reading.ingredients
          .map((i) => `<li><div class="chain-label">${esc(i)}</div></li>`)
          .join('')}</ol>`
      : '';

    // Styled by severity: a certificate we do not recognise is a caution, an
    // altered file is a hard failure. Showing both in red would say the same
    // thing about two very different situations.
    const warnClass = reading.verdict === 'tampered' ? 'warn-list' : 'warn-list warn-soft';
    const warnings = reading.warnings.length
      ? `<ul class="${warnClass}">${reading.warnings.map((w) => `<li>${esc(w)}</li>`).join('')}</ul>`
      : '';

    const TRUST: Record<Reading['signerTrust'], string | null> = {
      trusted: 'Recognised certificate',
      unrecognised: 'Not on the trust list',
      expired: 'Certificate expired',
      revoked: 'Certificate revoked',
    };

    const training =
      reading.aiTraining === 'not-allowed'
        ? 'The creator marked this as not available for AI training'
        : reading.aiTraining === 'allowed'
          ? 'The creator allows AI training on this'
          : null;

    return `
      <div class="result-head v-${reading.verdict}">
        <img class="thumb" src="${esc(thumbUrl)}" alt="" />
        <div class="verdict">
          <span class="verdict-tag">${TAGS[reading.verdict]}</span>
          <h2>${esc(reading.headline)}</h2>
          <p class="verdict-why">${esc(reading.explanation)}</p>
          <p class="confidence">${esc(CONFIDENCE[reading.confidence])}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      ${warnings}
      <div class="facts">
        ${fact('File', fileName)}
        ${fact('Signed by', reading.signer?.issuer ?? null)}
        ${fact('Certificate', reading.signer ? TRUST[reading.signerTrust] : null)}
        ${fact('Signed at', reading.signer?.time ? new Date(reading.signer.time).toLocaleString() : null)}
        ${fact('Made with', reading.producer)}
        ${fact('Recorded source', reading.sourceLabel)}
        ${fact('AI training', training)}
      </div>
      ${chain}
      ${ingredients}
      ${
        raw
          ? `<details class="raw"><summary>Show the raw manifest</summary><pre>${esc(
              JSON.stringify(raw, null, 2),
            )}</pre></details>`
          : ''
      }`;
  }

  let sdk: { reader: { fromBlob: (format: string, blob: Blob) => Promise<unknown> } } | null = null;

  /**
   * The C2PA engine is an 8MB WebAssembly binary, so it is fetched only when
   * someone actually checks a file. Loading it upfront would make the page
   * feel broken on a phone for people who never use it.
   */
  async function engine() {
    if (sdk) return sdk;
    const { createC2pa } = await import('@contentauth/c2pa-web');
    // No workerSrc: the library then runs its worker from a blob URL, which
    // works over plain http as well. Pointing workerSrc at our own copy is
    // only needed under a Content Security Policy that forbids blob workers,
    // and it rejects any non https URL, which breaks local development.
    sdk = (await createC2pa({ wasmSrc: '/c2pa/c2pa.wasm' })) as typeof sdk;
    return sdk;
  }

  async function check(file: File): Promise<void> {
    const thumbUrl = URL.createObjectURL(file);
    show('<div class="loading"><span class="spinner"></span>Reading the file on your device</div>');

    try {
      const c2pa = await engine();
      const reader = (await c2pa!.reader.fromBlob(file.type || 'image/jpeg', file)) as {
        manifestStore: () => Promise<unknown>;
      } | null;

      if (!reader) {
        show(render(interpret(null), thumbUrl, file.name, null));
        return;
      }

      const store = await reader.manifestStore();
      show(render(interpret(store as never), thumbUrl, file.name, store));
    } catch (error) {
      show(
        `<div class="failure"><div><strong>Could not read that file.</strong><br />${esc(
          (error as Error)?.message ?? 'Unknown error',
        )}</div></div>`,
      );
    } finally {
      result.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
    }
  }

  document.getElementById('try-sample')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    // Most people have never seen a file with credentials, so the tool would
    // otherwise only ever show them the "nothing found" result.
    const response = await fetch('/samples/signed-example.jpg');
    const blob = await response.blob();
    void check(new File([blob], 'signed-example.jpg', { type: 'image/jpeg' }));
  });

  drop.addEventListener('click', () => input.click());
  drop.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
    if ((event as KeyboardEvent).key === 'Enter' || (event as KeyboardEvent).key === ' ') {
      event.preventDefault();
      input.click();
    }
  });

  input.addEventListener('change', () => {
    const file = input.files?.[0];
    if (file) void check(file);
  });

  for (const type of ['dragenter', 'dragover']) {
    drop.addEventListener(type, (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      drop.classList.add('is-over');
    });
  }
  for (const type of ['dragleave', 'drop']) {
    drop.addEventListener(type, () => drop.classList.remove('is-over'));
  }

  drop.addEventListener('drop', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    const file = (event as DragEvent).dataTransfer?.files?.[0];
    if (file) void check(file);
  });
</script>
